WEBVTT

00:21:59.371 --> 00:22:01.746
let's talk about this or
that or vice versa,

00:22:01.996 --> 00:22:05.246
I feel like we almost
invariably end up in

00:22:05.246 --> 00:22:08.704
a place where there's something
that we are both, like,

00:22:08.704 --> 00:22:13.621
beaming about that we wouldn't have
arrived at had it just been one of us in

00:22:13.621 --> 00:22:18.663
that room. And in all likelihood, you know
, someone who looked like us,

00:22:18.663 --> 00:22:20.371
you know, either just me or just her.

00:22:20.371 --> 00:22:24.454
So I feel like there's a lot of
talk of how diversity is good

00:22:24.454 --> 00:22:26.496
and how you say in your book,
diversity is good but hard.

00:22:26.829 --> 00:22:30.038
But, you know, I have personally
felt like, you know,